{"type":"standard","title":"Isan language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Isan language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q33417","titles":{"canonical":"Isan_language","normalized":"Isan language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Isan language</span></span>"},"pageid":501222,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Isan_text.png/330px-Isan_text.png","width":330,"height":165},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dd/Isan_text.png","width":500,"height":250},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1355314078","tid":"01798b0b-54cc-11f1-ba79-6c561aa4faa7","timestamp":"2026-05-21T04:17:40Z","description":"Dialect of the Lao language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isan_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isan_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isan_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Isan_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isan_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Isan_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isan_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Isan_language"}},"extract":"Isan or Northeastern Thai refers to the local development of the Lao language in Thailand, after the political split of the Lao-speaking world at the Mekong River at the conclusion of the Franco-Siamese crisis of 1893. The language is still referred to as Lao by native speakers.","extract_html":"<p><b>Isan</b> or <b>Northeastern Thai</b> refers to the local development of the Lao language in Thailand, after the political split of the Lao-speaking world at the Mekong River at the conclusion of the Franco-Siamese crisis of 1893. The language is still referred to as <b>Lao</b> by native speakers.</p>"}